{
  "track": "es",
  "level": "A1",
  "unit": 23,
  "title": "Meat and fish",
  "description": "Name the meat and the fish, and say what is on the table.",
  "explanation": {
    "summary": "Meat and fish are the food words a learner needs before a restaurant, and they follow the ordinary rules: a noun with a gender, an article, and a plural.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "The nouns",
        "body": "La carne is feminine and means meat in general. El pollo and el cerdo are masculine, and so is el pescado, which means fish as food. La ternera is the meat of a young cow, and la gamba is a prawn. Nothing here breaks the rule: -a is feminine, -o is masculine.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "la carne",
            "en": "the meat"
          },
          {
            "es": "el pollo",
            "en": "the chicken"
          },
          {
            "es": "la gamba",
            "en": "the prawn"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "heading": "On the table",
        "body": "In a shop you ask for what you want with un or una, and the noun tells you the gender: un piece of chicken is un pollo, and a piece of fish is un pescado. In the plural the article changes too: dos gambas is not dos gamba.",
        "examples": [
          {
            "es": "un pescado con verduras",
            "en": "a fish with vegetables"
          },
          {
            "es": "dos gambas",
            "en": "two prawns"
          },
          {
            "es": "la ternasa está muy bien",
            "en": "the beef is very good"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
